      "choice": "protective stop is monitored manually in next() by comparing self.data.close[0] to a stored stop_price and issuing self.close() when breached, rather than submitting a native backtrader StopOrder",
      "reason": "spec requires the stop to optionally recompute each bar as a trailing stop, which is naturally expressed as a per-bar level check alongside the opposite-signal exit check; a static broker-side stop order could not be dynamically re-priced without cancel/resubmit each bar"
    },
    {
      "topic": "static vs trailing stop",
      "choice": "default is a static stop fixed at entry (atr_mult * ATR from entry_price, using the ATR value at the bar the entry order fills); a boolean parameter trailing_stop=False can be set True to instead ratchet the stop each bar (long stop only moves up, short stop only moves down) using the then-current ATR",
      "reason": "spec explicitly asks to specify in code whether stop is static (default) or optionally trailing via a parameter, but does not define the trailing update mechanics, so a standard one-directional ratchet was chosen"
